===Etymology===
{{compound|name|sake}}. From the phrase "(one's) [[name]]'s [[sake]]"; first recorded in the mid-seventeenth century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|nāmʹsāk}}, {{IPA|/ˈneɪmseɪk/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"neImseIk/}}
* {{audio|en-us-namesake.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who is [[name]]d after another or for whom another is named.<!--the original sense-->
# A person with the same name as another.

====Synonyms====
